    "title": "Powerball jackpot reaches $1 billion as Gulf Coast hopefuls dream big - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kate Sherman ,\n1 hours ago\nMOSS POINT, Miss. ( WKRG ) — The Powerball jackpot has climbed to an eye-popping $1 billion, sending hopeful players across the Gulf Coast out in search of their chance at life-changing money.\nJerry Carl wins GOP nomination in Alabama’s District 1 Special Congressional race At Keith’s in Moss Point, customers have been coming in throughout the day to grab their tickets and try their luck.\nFor the people buying those tickets, the excitement is about more than just what they could buy for themselves if they won.\nSeveral customers said their first priority would be helping family and friends.\nAnother customer makes the drive from Mobile to the Moss Point gas station every Saturday to try his luck.\nSo far, his biggest Powerball win has been about $14. But if he won the $1 billion jackpot, he already knows what he would do first.\nHe said he would help his best friend.\nFor everyone buying a ticket, though, it all comes down to the same thing: luck.\nOne hopeful player was asked whether he thought he might be holding the winning ticket.\n“I really hope so,” he said.\nAfter hearing what people would do with a billion dollars, there was only one thing left to do: buy a ticket.\nCoastal Alabama Community College in Mobile to expand aircraft maintenance program The Powerball drawing is Wednesday night.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WKRG News 5.",
